  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers the W3C response headers that lock down documents: Content Security Policy Level 3 (Working Draft of 16 September 2026, build posture) with directives, source lists, nonces and hashes, 'strict-dynamic', 'unsafe-hashes', report-to with Reporting-Endpoints, report-uri, Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only, frame-ancestors, upgrade-insecure-requests and the Strict CSP pattern; Trusted Types (require-trusted-types-for, trusted-types, policies, the default policy); Permissions Policy (the Permissions-Policy structured header, allowlists, the iframe allow attribute, report-only); and Fetch Metadata Request Headers (Sec-Fetch-Site, -Mode, -Dest, -User) with a server-side resource isolation policy. Version lines: CSP Level 3 current, CSP Level 2 supported, CSP 1.0 and its X-Content-Security-Policy and X-WebKit-CSP headers legacy; Trusted Types, Permissions Policy and Fetch Metadata each have one current line, with the Feature-Policy header legacy in the Permissions Policy family. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions and upgrades, CSP directives, strict CSP and reporting, Trusted Types, Permissions Policy, and Fetch Metadata.",
